Hello, Mythbusters!

It’s been a busy time since the premiere last week. You’ve spoken up, and we’re patching! 

First of all, we’ve heard that some of you experience a problem with a black screen when you launch the game. We have a possible quick fix: open the game folder and delete all the saves there. Let us know if it helped you!

[b]Here are the issues we will be addressing in the next patch:[/b]

[list][*]After a game restart, Buster appears in our hands;
[*]Incorrect location description after selecting the “see details” option – the truck;
[*]Issue with an incorrect camera placement while assembling the elements;
[*]The checklist might display incorrect information in the Impossible Fuel myth;
[*]If the rocket is flying too fast, the altitude indicator on the monitor at the launch pad while the rocket is flying is blurred;
[*]The indicator on the pumping station screen is blurred and smudged;
[*]The Checklist in the Is it a bird? Is it a chair? myth is updating incorrectly;
[*]If we switch off the game while holding an item in our hands, the item will be invisible after logging back in;
[*]The rocket storage location on the training grounds disappears when it is at the edge of the field of view;
[*]In the Rocket Car myth, if the ramp is fully extended, the paint roller may lose interactivity;
[*]Incorrect advice on how to hammer nails in Spanish;
[*]In Japanese and Chinese, the names of locations are dark;
[*]In Japanese, the riddle answer is incorrect;
[*]In Chinese, the texts may be overlapping slightly;
[*]In Japanese, some of the journal texts in the Impossible Fuel overlap with the dots underneath them which reduces readability;
[*]In Korean, page headers in the journal go outside the lines or overlap;
[*]In Korean, titles in the journal’s table of content overlap;
[*]Items bought during the experiment after the cleanup were still in their places but were invisible;
[*]Players cannot click buttons in the game, especially the yellow ones.[/list]

Keep your feedback coming, stay tuned!
